fact WorkItem(id: "WI-245", description: some(value: "Parse-IR Expr/Term split. Currently parse/ir.rs has a single SimpleTermStore (Vec<ParseTermEntry { term, span }>) and convert.rs's convert_term family produces TermId for every position — expression bodies (operation body, lambda body, conditional branches, match arms, let bodies) and KB-position references (fact bodies, rule heads) flow through the same uniform Term IR. This conflates two fundamentally different identity semantics: KB positions are structural (hash-consed, sharing wanted); expression positions are positional (each source occurrence is distinct, sharing catastrophic). The Handle-wrapper hack in load.rs:3307 (Term::Const(Literal::Handle(Occurrence, occ_id))) exists only to prevent hash-cons collapse of expression-position content — wrapping each occurrence's content in a unique Handle defeats the hash-cons. WI-245 fixes this at the parse IR boundary: introduce an  recursive value type (NO ExprId — Expr children are owned via Vec<Expr>; inline Span; no arena, no hash-cons because there's nothing to share). Variants mirror expression forms: Var, Const, Apply { functor, pos_args, named_args }, Lambda, Let, Match, If, etc. Item types in parse/ir.rs update: Operation.body: Option<TermId> -> Option<Expr>; Lambda/Match/Let/If branches similarly. Add convert_expr_* family in parse/convert.rs that mirrors convert_term_* but produces Expr. Tree-sitter grammar unchanged. The loader's convert_expr_term (load.rs:3275) adapts to consume Expr from parse IR (was: TermId); produces the same KB-side output (Handle-wrapped TermId + OccurrenceEntry) as today — no KB-layer behavior change. Prerequisite for WI-242: with the parse-IR split landed, WI-242 reduces to KB-side work (loader allocates KB Expr in OccurrenceStore directly; Value::Expr; TermView::ViewItem::Occurrence; delete Handle wrapper). Out of scope: KB-side Expr (WI-242), HandleKind::Occurrence removal (WI-242), Value::Expr (WI-242). Estimated ~300-400 LOC, mostly in parse/ir.rs and parse/convert.rs. Acceptance: cargo-test green; existing test behavior preserved; new Expr round-trip tests pass."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-241"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-15T17:14:41Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-245", author: "user", content: "SUPERSEDED by design refinement (see docs/design/occurrence-as-value-type.md). Initial scope was 'parse-IR Expr split — introduce Expr enum at parse layer, change Operation.body to Option<Expr>'. After extended design discussion, the parse-IR layer is staying UNCHANGED: Item enum, all existing struct types (Namespace, Operation, Fact, Rule, etc.), TermId/SimpleTermStore — all keep their current shape. The Expr/Term distinction happens at the KB layer instead, via WI-242 introducing NodeOccurrence + NodeKind + Expr value types and eliminating OccurrenceStore/OccurrenceId/Handle wrapper. WI-245's parse-side refactor is no longer needed because the loader does the routing at the KB boundary, walking parse-IR Items and producing KB-side NodeOccurrence for expression-position content vs KB-side Term for KB-position content. No code landed for this WI. Marking delivered with this supersession note for traceability.", at: "2026-05-15T17:14:40Z")
